<title>UK: Aluminium stocks down in September - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks down in September - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.257 million tonnes at the end of September 1996, compared with an upwardly revised 3.353 million in August and 3.685 million in September 1995, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.747 million tonnes versus 1.838 million and 2.082 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Sept 96   Aug 96   Sept 95</p>
<p>    Africa		    67	 88	  62</p>
<p>    North America	1,548    1,568     1,721</p>
<p>    Latin America	  182	200	 201</p>
<p>    Asia		     159	170	 176</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,173    1,196     1,363</p>
<p>    Oceania		  128	131	 162</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Sept 96   Aug 96   Sept 95</p>
<p>    Africa		   22	  44	  24</p>
<p>    North America	 721	 727	 841</p>
<p>    Latin America	 133	 152	 147</p>
<p>    Asia		    132	 139	 150</p>
<p>    Europe		  647	 679	 806</p>
<p>    Oceania		  92	  97	 114</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8065</p>
